{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Reached the constructor stall through a live cluster instead of a supplied fixture, which was the main remaining premise of that question. The new harness runs a three-node cluster {A,B,C} in memory with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs enabled on every node, elects B, commits five entries, takes a user snapshot on A at index 6, commits 250 further entries so A's staged commit index reaches 257, shuts A down while B and C keep a quorum, and then restarts A from its own stores with MaxAppendEntries 1. Local construction feedback is deterministic across three runs: the feature-on restart does not return within the 5s window, the cluster stays alive without A, and the identical restart without the feature returns as a follower with lastApplied still at the snapshot index.\\\",\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"e99a162d27c7421fa6729d8cb9703581-question-1\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_live_replay_stall_test.go\\\",\\\"execution_package\\\":\\\".\\\",\n  \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"7fa5f1ed17f8424c8920cf921834e074-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"Reaches the same stall through ordinary cluster operations rather than a harness-supplied fixture: a follower accumulates a staged commit index far above its last snapshot by running with the feature and then restarting with a small MaxAppendEntries; the comparison set is limited to the new scenario's predicates and the earlier predicates remain with their own receipts.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"New harness file: a three-node in-memory cluster with the feature enabled, a user snapshot on one follower, 250 further committed entries, a graceful shutdown of that follower and two restart attempts from its own stores.\\\",\n   \\\"The stalled restart uses MaxAppendEntries 1 so 251 entries above the snapshot need 251 batches, and the control restart uses the same stores with the feature off.\\\"],\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-restorecommitted\\\",\\\"s-processlogs\\\",\\\"s-fsmch\\\",\\\"s-startup-order\\\",\\\"s-staging\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Live three-node cluster (A, B, C; in-memory transports and stores; timeouts scaled to 50ms) in which node A runs with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs enabled, is snapshotted early at index 6, receives 250 further committed entries so its staged commit index is 257, is shut down while B and C retain a quorum, and is then restarted twice from its own stores: once with the feature and MaxAppendEntries 1, once with the feature off.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Every state that matters is produced by normal operations: bootstrap {A,B,C} from A, leader election with leadership transferred to B if needed, committed applies, a user-triggered Snapshot on A, further committed applies, and a graceful Shutdown of A.\\\",\n    \\\"The feature is enabled on all three nodes during the first life, which is the deployment mode whose restart behaviour is under test; this is what makes the commit-tracking store hold a persisted commit index for A.\\\",\n    \\\"A's snapshot index stays at 6 because SnapshotInterval is 10 minutes and the harness takes no further snapshot on A, so the replay must cover 251 entries.\\\",\n    \\\"Non-return is evaluated by constructing in a goroutine and waiting 5s; the control uses the same stores with the feature off so fixture size, store speed and cluster state are excluded as causes.\\\",\n    \\\"The stalled constructor is abandoned; a fresh transport is created for each restart attempt and the peers are reconnected to it.\\\"],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No crash, on-disk store or process kill is exercised; A is shut down gracefully.\\\",\n    \\\"The stalled instance is not resumed and no application-level timeout or supervision is modelled.\\\",\n    \\\"No repository test was executed.\\\"],\n   \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"cluster_ids\\\":\\\"A,B,C\\\",\\\"snapshot_index\\\":6,\\\"staged_commit_index\\\":257,\\\"entries_to_replay\\\":251,\\\"max_append_entries_on_restart\\\":1,\\\"observation_window_seconds\\\":5}},\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness builds three InmemTransports (A, B, C) in a full mesh with per-node InmemStore (stable), InmemCommitTrackingStore (logs) and InmemSnapshotStore (snapshots); it bootstraps {A,B,C} from A with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs enabled, starts A, B and C with MockFSM, waits for a leader and transfers leadership to B if another node won. It applies five commands on the leader, waits until A's applied index is at least four, then takes a user snapshot on A (index 6). It applies 250 further commands, waits until A's log store reports a staged commit index of at least 156, and emits a 'fixture' event with the snapshot index, the staged commit index, A's log last index, the number of entries the replay would cover, whether that exceeds the 128-slot channel, the cluster ids and the leader. It shuts A down, confirms the other two nodes still have a leader, and emits 'cluster_status' with whether the cluster is alive without A and whether the stalled restart returned. Each restart attempt creates a fresh transport for A, reconnects the peers, and calls NewRaft in a goroutine with a bounded window: 'stalled_restart' uses Config.RestoreCommittedLogs and MaxAppendEntries 1, 'control_restart' uses the same stores with the feature off. A 'control_restart_summary' event records the control's return and applied index. Event order: fixture, stalled_restart, cluster_status, control_restart, control_restart_summary.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"hashicorp/raft NewRaft startup path: restoreFromCommittedLogs replays committed entries through processLogs into fsmMutateCh before the constructor starts the only consumer, runFSM.\\\",\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"8001bad80a4d4ef0a840634644afdf63-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"NewRaft cannot return when the replay needs more batches than the 128-slot fsmMutateCh holds\\\"}],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"adm_live\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"fixture\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"live_restart_after_long_gap\\\"},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshot_index\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":6},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"staged_commit_index\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":257},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"entries_to_replay\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":251},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"gap_over_channel\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]}],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"stalled_restart\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_live\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"live_restart_after_long_gap\\\"}],\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"newraft_returned\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"description\\\":\\\"A follower restarted with the feature over 251 committed entries should finish NewRaft within the observation window.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"control_restart\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_live\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"live_restart_after_long_gap\\\"}],\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"newraft_returned\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the same stores restarted without the feature should construct normally.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"control_restart\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_live\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"live_restart_after_long_gap\\\"}],\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"last_applied\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":6},\\\"description\\\":\\\"Control operand: without the replay the FSM stays at the snapshot index, so the difference is the replay and not the gap itself.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"cluster_status\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_live\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"live_restart_after_long_gap\\\"}],\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"cluster_alive_without_a\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"description\\\":\\\"The remaining two voters keep a quorum while the restarted node cannot start, so the stall is not a cluster-wide outage in this size.\\\"}]\n }}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run && cp draft/work/zz_live_test.go draft/assurance_live_replay_stall_test.go && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
