\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"live_restart_after_long_gap\\\"}],\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"last_applied\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":6},\\\"description\\\":\\\"Control operand: without the replay the FSM stays at the snapshot index, so the difference is the replay and not the gap itself.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"cluster_status\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_live\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"live_restart_after_long_gap\\\"}],\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"cluster_alive_without_a\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"description\\\":\\\"The remaining two voters keep a quorum while the restarted node cannot start, so the stall is not a cluster-wide outage in this size.\\\"}]\n }}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run && cp draft/work/zz_live_test.go draft/assurance_live_replay_stall_test.go && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"written\n{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"c616cad1b86d42518c7af4bc5bffef9d\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 2023.0867467539997, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": true, \"effects\": [{\"object\": \"experiments\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"experiment\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Filed a live-cluster witness for the constructor-stall question, whose main remaining premise was that its fixture was harness-supplied. The new harness grows a three-node in-memory cluster {A,B,C} with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs enabled on every node, elects B, commits five entries, takes a user snapshot on A at index 6, commits 250 further entries so A's staged commit index reaches 257, shuts A down while B and C keep a quorum, and restarts A from its own stores twice: with the feature and MaxAppendEntries 1, then without the feature. Local construction feedback was deterministic across three runs: the feature-on restart never returned within the 5s window while the cluster stayed alive without A, and the identical restart without the feature returned as a follower with lastApplied still at the snapshot index, so the replay rather than the gap or the stores explains the stall. The experiment is filed as a revision of that question's earlier experiment (same investigation) with an admission pinning the fixture operands (snapshot 6, staged commit 257, 251 entries to replay, gap over the channel) and four comparisons covering the stalled restart, the control restart, the control's applied index and the surviving quorum. Incomplete: that receipt and its interpretation, the user Restore and term-changing truncation repair paths, a long-run window over the divergent state, and whether the operational frequency of such a gap makes the stall likely in practice.\"}"}}
